+# 回归报告 / Regression Report
+
+Minecraft execution callbacks deliberately avoid persisting spoken plans as
+task evidence. This also discarded all memory of their wording: a second
+callback could not see a completed first reply. In the observed local session,
+46 main-brain replies contained five exact duplicate groups (eight extra
+replies); the separate playback trace showed no duplicate playback cycles.
+
+The execution callback now keeps a session-local speech recency cache: at most
+four quotes, 240 characters each, expiring after five minutes. Only committed,
+non-cancelled speech enters it. A request-only note labels quotes as prior
+speech, without authority or evidence of task acceptance, actions, completion
+or rewards. The actual human instructions, tool receipts and persistent
+conversation history are retained. Ordinary dialogue and foreign callbacks
+do not receive this cache. There are no additional model calls, tool actions,
+playback filters or persistent transcript copies.
+
+The reproduction initially failed because the second request contained zero
+references to the first spoken reply. The corrected integration and boundary
+tests cover request projection, bounded/expired quotes, isolation, silent tool
+turns, actual receipts and stop instructions. The focused set passed 160 tests
+with one known logger-capture test deselected. The broader speech/tool suite
+passed 2,134 tests and reproduced that same pre-existing logger-capture failure
+(`test_failed_takeover_with_stale_token_still_unmutes`), previously reproduced
+on the unmodified baseline. No broader pass is claimed.
+
+Potential regressions: the request gains up to roughly 1,700 characters at its
+dynamic tail, and a model could still repeat or over-interpret its own words.
+The explicit non-evidence label and original no-persistence test cover the
+boundary; natural-session speech quality and task progress require separate
+observation. Do not close gameplay or audible-quality tickets on these tests.
